From 4c3c949324c9b764db886d14a63383ff68af0f7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liyuan <liyuan390@huawei.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:20:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(control): prepare a managed run without spawning and
 let a host adopt it

Extract the record-creating half of start_run() into prepare_run(), which
returns a PreparedRun and starts nothing, and keep start_run() as prepare plus
the detached spawn inside the same registry lock so the existing start/stop/
resume behaviour is unchanged.

supervise() now claims an unset pid/process_created under the directory lock
itself and refuses an identity that belongs to another process. It accepts two
additive host hooks -- an in-process stop_event and an on_ready callback -- and,
when a stop event is given, short-circuits into a positive not-started record
and arms exactly one control task that cancels the bound supervisor once,
cancelled and awaited in finally on every exit path. A stop consumed while
reports are generating keeps the research outcome and states the report as
incomplete instead of escaping as an unrecorded cancellation.

The expensive boundaries stay substitutable: run_manifest is a module attribute
resolved lazily, and the report generator is imported from its own module.
