+"""Supervisor for one managed run; no terminal or interactive CLI ownership.
+
+The same entry point serves two hosts:
+
+* the CLI launches this module as a detached session, which adopts the record
+  the launcher already owns through the PID it recorded;
+* a host that owns a supervised process (a sandbox bootstrap) prepares the run
+  with ``service.prepare_run()`` and then calls :func:`supervise` in that
+  process. The record has no PID yet, so the supervisor claims it here under
+  the directory lock, and the host may hand in the two additive hooks it needs:
+  an in-process ``stop_event`` and an ``on_ready`` callback. A supervisor that
+  claims nothing (another process's token or identity) returns without touching
+  the record, so a second attempt never overwrites an owner.
+"""
 
